Subject: Re: [S] MANOVAs and ANOVAs with repeated measures (summary)
In-Reply-To: <199802131445.IAA02850@wubios.wustl.edu>
Message-ID: <s4e420d0.020@pgh.auhs.edu>

In S+ 4, there is a section in the Guide to Statisitcs manual  (p 433) on the 
MANOVA approach to repeated measures designs.  You simply post-multiply your 
response matrix by the (orthogonal) repeated measures contrast matrix in the 
formlua to MANOVA (p 434).

Let Y (n x p) be the reponse matrix with design matrix X.  Assume you want 
polynomial contrasts.  Then you use

maonva(Y %*% contr.poly(p) ~ X).

The univariate tests are available as an option to the summary() function. 

There is also an example of the Huynh-Feldt  adjustment.

If you need more detail, write.

Joe

