Dear Cassie:

You might try looking at a transformation of the dependent
variable.

Also check for serial correlation via the Durbin Watson 
statistic.

If you get a chance, you might want to take a look at
Draper & Smith's "Applied Regression Analysis".  Appendix
2c discusses "How significant should my regression be?"
This is in the second edition, from 1981.  Authors:
Norman Draper and Harry Smith.

This book has details on the suggestions that I made.

I hope this helps!

