Message-ID: <9802190243.AA01559@uhdux2.dt.uh.edu>

Dear David:

Watcom is still the compiler for S+ 4.

I have Watcom FORTRAN Version 11, which is the latest
version, and it is still only FORTRAN 77.

The only snag from one compiler to the other that I have 
found is the WRITE statement in FORTRAN....it
won't work in S+.  If your routines use WRITE, or PRINT,
they will compile, but they won't run in S+.

The way around that is to use the CALL REALPR for reals,
CALL INTPR for integers, or CALL DBLEPR for double precisions.

Please check your S+ help for more info on those.

Everything else should be ok.

I hope this helps!

Sincerely,
